David Ernst

Usage:
    convert-images [options] <inputDir> <outputDir>
Options:
    -h, --help      Print this help page.
    -c, --crop      crop excessive whitespace
    -a, --always    convert every image, including one whose file size says it is
                    already starved. Without it such an image is left alone: see
                    below.
    -r, --reverse   reverse: convert the -o format back to jpeg
    -o, --format <format>
                    output format: avif, webp or jxl, default avif
    -j, --jobs <jobs>
                    Run up to <jobs> encoder processes in parallel.
                    Only needed when RAM is short, otherwise a good guess is made.
    -q, --quality <quality>
                    quality level of the output images
    -s, --speed <speed>
                    av1 speed preset 0-9, lower is slower, default 5
    -m, --max-resolution <maxRes>
                    maximum resolution (height) to keep
    -f, --fuzz <fuzz>
                    when trimming, how many percent color difference gets still trimmed
